  "notes": "Acoustic-soul pop with rhythmic scat-phrasing: 65–100 straight with the backbeat on 2&4, and the ubiquitous 2008 single is \"a reggae-inflected 76 with the accent on the off-beat\" — which is why `bpm.mode` sits at 76 and why the percussion `placement` is \"offbeat\". The drum block is the entry's most unusual in this batch because the hat is replaced: \"off-beat guitar skank taking the place of a hat, shaker in 8ths\", so `hihat.continuous` is false at a 0.2 fill density while the perc block runs shaker, rim and conga at 3–6. The other two deltas are \"kick 1 and 3, snare/rim on 2&4\" and \"brush fills only\", i.e. a soft velocity tier and a fill schedule pushed out to 16 bars. Harmony is major with jazz-pop extensions — I–V–vi–IV with maj7/6 voicings and a ii–V turnaround — so the sevenths and ninths carry 0.62 between them. The bass is \"roots with a walking passing note into each change; upright-bass feel\", which is `independent_riff` at 0.7 with the widest passing-tone set here. The vocal is described as \"the rhythm instrument — syllable-dense, syncopated, scatted between phrases, with a wide-interval hook\", which is the 6–12 density and the raised leap share. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research says so and marks the key/voicing claims **[LOW-CONF]** as convention-based. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities.",
